{"records":[{"id":"rb663c2bgg","title":"Dataset on the Design and Functional Evaluation of INHBE-Targeting Small Interfering RNAs","description":"This dataset provides experimental data on the design, chemical screening, in vitro transcription, and functional evaluation of INHBE-targeting small interfering RNAs. The dataset includes siRNA target-site design information, chemical siRNA screening data, DNA template sequences and IVT-derived siRNA information, comparative functional evaluation data, and supporting RT-qPCR information. The dataset supports the associated Data in Brief article and provides sequence information and processed experimental data for the evaluation of INHBE-targeting siRNAs.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-09-29T13:01:20.731Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/rb663c2bgg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/rb663c2bgg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"TONG","last_name":"LUZIYUN","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Methodology in Biological Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wwh3xkym9s","title":"Cholesterol-dependent control of endosomal escape regulates intracellular trafficking of small interfering RNA therapeutics and interactions with small molecule drugs","description":"This dataset includes raw and processed measurements examining how modulation of intracellular cholesterol alters the efficacy of FDA-approved siRNA therapeutics. Data are structured according to experimental variables, including cell model, cholesterol manipulation strategy, siRNA treatment, and target suppression quantified at both the mRNA and protein levels.\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-01-14T10:43:24.442Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/wwh3xkym9s","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/wwh3xkym9s"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Sherouk","last_name":"Tawfik","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/04q48ey07","name":"National Institute of General Medical Sciences","grant_id":"R35GM140862"}],"categories":["Cholesterol","Small Interfering RNA"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"2m9mf7rs8k","title":"Parametric Data Study of High-k Gate with Dielectric Pocket(DP) Gate All Around(GAA) FETs ","description":"This paper presents the parameteric data study of the High-k Gate stack with Dielectric Pocket(DP) Gate All Around(GAA) FETs. A High K gate stack and dielectric pockets inside the channel have been used as a performance booster in the device. Dielectric pockets reduce the off current, and a high K gate stacking improves the on current. Both are the critical parameter to evaluate a MOSFET.Reduction in off current reduce the power decipation in off state and increment in on current improves the device speed.Parametric data study has been done for on current(Ion), off current(Ioff), DIBL and transconductance. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-10-08T10:39:54.393Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/2m9mf7rs8k","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/2m9mf7rs8k"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Shubham ","last_name":"Yadav","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Vaibhav ","last_name":"Purwar","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Manish Kumar","last_name":"Dixit","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Field Effect Transistors"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"6dbgkhzxvx","title":"Data for: The effect of temperature on toxicokinetics and the chronic toxicity of insecticides towards Gammarus pulex","description":"Raw data for the study \"The effect of temperature on toxicokinetics and the chronic toxicity of insecticides toward Gammarus pulex\" and \"Explicit consideration of temperature improves predictions of toxicokinetic-toxicodynamic models for flupyradifurone and imidacloprid in Gammarus pulex\". ","source":{"id":"3a81646c-09ab-4bf8-b183-d0f2664e2a94","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-06-07T15:13:08.439Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/6dbgkhzxvx","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/6dbgkhzxvx"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Anna","last_name":"Huang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Annika","last_name":"Mangold-Döring","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Huitong","last_name":"Guan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Marie-Claire","last_name":"Boerwinkel","orcid":null},{"first_name":" Dick","last_name":"Belgers","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Andreas","last_name":"Focks","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Paul","last_name":"van den Brink","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Toxicokinetics","Aquatic Invertebrates","Toxicity","Temperature","Insecticide"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"5m66xtv4wg","title":"Safeguard DCL2-Dependent 22-nt siRNA Generation by DCL1 data","description":"In plants, miRNAs and siRNAs are crucial for their growth and development via mediating post-transcriptional gene silencing. In wild-type Arabidopsis, DCL2-dependent 22-nt siRNAs are rare, whereas DCL1- and DCL4-dependent 21-nt miRNAs and siRNAs are highly abundant. DCL4 naturally inhibits DCL2 in producing abundant 22-nt siRNAs from endogenous transcripts, but whether DCL1 suppresses endogenous 22-nt siRNA production and the extent of the DCL1-mediated repression of DCL2 activity are still unknown. To address these issues, we used small sequencing technologies to investigate the potential mechanism for the critical roles of DCL1 and DCL4 in protecting plant growth from the disturbing of DCL2-dependent 22-nt siRNAs.\nArabidopsis mutants used in this study, dcl1-9 (CS3828) is in the Ler background, and the others are all in the Col-0 background, including dcl2-1 (SALK_064627.42.50.x), dcl4-2 (GABI_160G05), and dcl2-1 dcl4-2t (N66078; CS66078). Other double and triple mutants including dcl1-9 dcl2-1, dcl1-9 dcl4-2, and dcl1-9 dcl2-1 dcl4-2t were generated by genetic crossing.\nOur data showed that DCL1 and DCL2 cleaved both miRNA precursors and coding transcript-derived double-stranded RNAs in Arabidopsis defective for both DCL1 and DCL4. In the dcl1 dcl4 double mutant, massive 22-nt siRNAs broke the RNA-decay safeguard were produced by endogenous protein-coding genes (genic siRNAs), of which NIA1, NIA2, DGAT3, and both SMXL4 and SMXL5 accumulated the abundance of 22-nt siRNAs up to 95%. These 22-nt genic siRNAs were likely loaded into AGO1 or AGO2 and further mediated gene translation repression. Thus, our results demonstrated that both DCL1 and DCL4 safeguard post-transcriptional gene silencing, preventing the production of DCL2-dependent 22-nt genic siRNAs from disturbing plant growth and development. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-03-14T09:11:58.682Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/5m66xtv4wg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/5m66xtv4wg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Dongdong","last_name":"Lu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Li","last_name":"Feng","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jixian","last_name":"Zhai","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Bosheng","last_name":"Li","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mengli","last_name":"Xi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["microRNA","Small Interfering RNA"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"kcxrcxmbms","title":"Global Mapping of circRNA-Target RNA Interactions Reveals P-Body-Mediated Translational Repression","description":"Original data of gels  blots and microscopy of Global Mapping of circRNA-Target RNA Interactions Reveals P-Body-Mediated Translational Repression","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-02-09T05:08:54.421Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/kcxrcxmbms","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/kcxrcxmbms"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"yuanchao","last_name":"xue","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Circular RNA"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"dt2ncczrms","title":"Dismissal of RNA Polymerase II Underlies a Large Ligand-induced Enhancer Decommissioning Program","description":"Nuclear receptors induce both transcriptional activation and repression programs responsible for development, homeostasis, and disease. Here, we report a previously overlooked enhancer decommissioning strategy underlying a large estrogen receptor alpha (ERα)-dependent transcriptional repression program. The unexpected signature for this E2-induced program resides in indirect recruitment of ERα to a large cohort of pioneer factor basally active FOXA1-bound enhancers that lack cognate ERα DNA-binding elements. Surprisingly, these basally active estrogen-repressed (BAER) enhancers are decommissioned by ERα-dependent recruitment of the histone demethylase KDM2A, functioning independently of its demethylase activity. Rather, KDM2A tethers the E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase NEDD4 to ubiquitylate/dismiss Pol II to abrogate eRNA transcription, with consequent target gene downregulation. Thus, our data reveal that Pol II ubiquitylation/dismissal may serve as a potentially broad strategy utilized by indirectly bound nuclear receptors to abrogate large programs of pioneer factor-mediated, eRNA-producing enhancers.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-10-02T16:28:51.832Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/dt2ncczrms","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/dt2ncczrms"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yuliang","last_name":"Tan","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":["10972765"]},{"id":"v2cmt87777","title":"CMCSENet","description":"RGB-IR object detection effectively improves the robustness of object detection in complex scenarios by fusing the texture information of visible images and the thermal radiation information of infrared images. However, existing multimodal detection methods still face two key challenges. On the one hand, single-modality features and fused features often contain target responses, background interference, and local noise simultaneously. Directly extracting multi-scale contextual information from such entangled features is not only inefficient, but also prone to introducing noise interference. On the other hand, cross modal feature fusion is easily affected by modality discrepancies, pseudo thermal sources, and texture blur, which weakens the reliability and discriminability of fused semantics. To address these issues, we proposes a Cross Modal Context and Semantic Enhancement Network (CMCSENet). Specifically, we design a Region Guided Context Modeling Block (RGCMB), which organizes complex features into clearer candidate region representations through region guided mapping, and combines main context kernels with sparse context sub-kernels in the context modeling branches to simultaneously enhance local target details, regional structures, and large-range semantic consistency. Furthermore, we propose a Cross Modal Semantic Enhancement Module (CSEM), which progressively calibrates fused features from four aspects, namely modality response preservation, statistical semantic modeling, spatial structure enhancement, and frequency discriminative screening. In this way, cross modal noise and irrelevant background responses are suppressed, and the stability and discriminability of fused features are improved. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-07-08T17:04:10.469Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/v2cmt87777","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/v2cmt87777"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Guoquan","last_name":"Guo","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Object Detection","Feature Fusion"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"d3p8zdz6mp","title":"Figure1A_siRNAscreen_NF-kB","description":"Dataset for siRNA screen of NF-kB target genes, 156 genes in total","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-22T17:40:15.377Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/d3p8zdz6mp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/d3p8zdz6mp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Benjamin","last_name":"Nilsson-Payant","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Nuclear Factor Kappa B","Differential Gene Expression","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"36dd4gd83x","title":"Research Data for Data-Guided Operating-Window Mapping of SHP-Catalyzed Pummerer’s Ketone Formation","description":"This dataset contains the experimental and computational data supporting the manuscript entitled “Data-Guided Operating-Window Mapping for Soybean Hull Peroxidase-Catalyzed Pummerer’s Ketone Formation: Multiscale Interpretation of Selectivity”. The dataset includes the 200-observation experimental dataset used for random-forest modeling, prospective model-validation data, time-resolved chromatographic profiles, early-stage H₂O₂-dependent reaction data, and selected numerical results from molecular dynamics and multiscale computational analyses. The data are provided to support transparency, reproducibility, and reuse of the reported results.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-10-15T15:01:19.203Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/36dd4gd83x","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/36dd4gd83x"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Liang","last_name":"Zhou","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xiujuan","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Peng","last_name":"Yu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Gao","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yuanyuan","last_name":"Zhang","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":null,"name":"Shandong Provincial Natural Science Foundation","grant_id":"ZR2025QC1319"},{"id":null,"name":"Shandong Provincial Natural Science Foundation","grant_id":"ZR2023MB121"}],"categories":["Biochemistry","Chemical Engineering"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":142534,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":196,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":142534,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":141725,"restricted":71,"embargoed":738},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2362},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1378},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":712},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":479},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":443},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":431},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"Conselho Nacional de Desenvolvimento Científico e Tecnológico","count":417},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":399},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":319},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":282}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":139871},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1909},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":186},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":140},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":78},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":66},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":58},{"id":"b121dfec-bb51-4f19-a2f6-bc9ce0197286","name":"Babeș-Bolyai University","count":43},{"id":"7e51a2dd-133e-43c6-a220-12c1958e202a","name":"University of Canberra","count":32},{"id":"f2ed6517-7fb4-4e02-8cef-95e75e9f0c9d","name":"Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University","count":27}],"top_institutions_stats":[{"id":"ecb64011-71f0-5223-b4e4-4d27d5f51d83","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid Centro de Biologia Molecular Severo Ochoa","count":896},{"id":"9d63ad1d-c391-5c35-a12e-cafe17017098","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid","count":842},{"id":"3bfef41a-d03e-5722-bd55-dd245235fa78","name":"Bina Nusantara University","count":541},{"id":"0ad97c43-5173-56e6-bbe6-46dad5323862","name":"Daffodil International University","count":409},{"id":"55ba66b2-f276-5204-a3d8-acfa499794e0","name":"The University of Manchester","count":373}]}}